editorialMd:
The working idea

links is a symmetric 0/1 adjacency matrix. Union every connected pair, then produce the size of the component containing each vertex, in vertex order. Self-links do not change a component.

Return the largest value in the derived sequence, or 0 for an empty sequence. Negative maxima must remain negative.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(V^2 alpha(V)); space O(n).

javascript
function cableFamiliesPeakTicket(links, k) {
  const a=links; let out=[];
  const n=a.length,parent=Array.from({length:n},(_,i)=>i),size=Array(n).fill(1);function find(x){while(parent[x]!==x){parent[x]=parent[parent[x]];x=parent[x];}return x;}for(let u=0;u<n;u++)for(let v=u+1;v<n;v++)if(a[u][v]){let x=find(u),y=find(v);if(x!==y){if(size[x]<size[y])[x,y]=[y,x];parent[y]=x;size[x]+=size[y];}}out=parent.map((_,v)=>size[find(v)]);
  let answer=out.length?out[0]:0;for(const x of out)if(x>answer)answer=x;return answer;
}


